  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A significant fire occurred on November 19, 2026, in the Baduy Luar indigenous settlement in Cipaler, Banten, impacting dozens of households. According to initial reports, the fire destroyed 19 residential structures as well as two communal rice granaries and other traditional storage buildings. The incident has left numerous families displaced, with estimates suggesting that between 34 and 44 families have been directly affected by the disaster. In response to the emergency, Banten Governor Andra Soni has mandated that local disaster management agencies provide immediate relief and coordinate a rapid recovery effort for the community. The fire adds to a series of recent structural blazes reported across the region, though this event is specifically focused on the traditional village area of Desa Kanekes in the Leuwidamar district.",
